  "title": "weekly-updates: Fix running tool scripts under Windows",
  "description": "As the Python documentation warns, \"On all platforms, passing\nsys.executable is the recommended way to launch the current\nPython interpreter again.\" On Windows, this is necessary because\nPython scripts may not be directly executable, but it also is\nuseful on other platforms, e.g. to run the same Python interpreter\ninstead of another one that might be earlier in the PATH.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
